{
  "methodology": "Naive agent scored by applying its deterministic logic exactly as implemented in harness/agents/naive_agent.py. Claude and Gemini diagnoses are both collected via direct API calls (harness/run_claude_diagnoses.py, harness/run_gemini_diagnoses.py) using the identical closed-book prompt, run by the user in their own environment since this sandbox blocks authenticated calls to both api.anthropic.com and generativelanguage.googleapis.com. Both arms are graded via harness/run_llm_judge.py, a standalone port of harness/scoring/rca_judge.py's LLMDiagnosisJudge and JUDGE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE, wired to real API calls with genuine cross-model judging: Gemini grades Claude's diagnoses, Claude grades Gemini's diagnoses, so no model ever grades its own answers. This resolves both the automation gap and the grader-independence gap noted in every prior version of this report. Scoring formula (unchanged): overall = (0.6*causal_chain_coverage + 0.4*required_elements_coverage) * distractor_penalty, where distractor_penalty = 1 - 0.5*fraction_of_distractors_asserted_as_cause.",
